  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Living in Iowa ( (爱荷华州) ) and trying to become a {photographer} {specializing} in {landscape} can be quite a challenge, {mainly} because the {corn} state lacks {geographical variation} .",
      "cn": "住在爱荷华州，并努力成为一名 专门拍摄风景 的 摄影师 ，可谓是一个不小的挑战， 主要 是因为这个 玉米 之州缺乏 地理上的多样性 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Although landscapes in the Midwest {tend} to be quite similar, either {farm} fields or highways, sometimes I find {distinctive} character in the {hills} or {lakes} .To make some of my landscape shots, I have traveled up to four hours away to {shoot} within a 10-minute time frame.I tend to travel with a {few} of my friends to state {parks} or to the {countryside} to go on adventures and take {photos along} the way.",
      "cn": "虽然中西部的风景 往往 颇为相似，要么是 农 田，要么是公路，但有时我也能在 山丘 或 湖泊 中发现 独特的 景致。为了拍摄一些风景照，我曾驱车长达四个小时，只为在10分钟的时间范围内进行 拍摄 。我通常会和 几个 朋友一起前往州立 公园 或 乡村 探险， 沿 途拍 照 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "Being at the right place at the right time is {decisive} in any style of {photography} .I often leave early to {seek} the right {destinations} so I can set up early to avoid missing the moment I am {attempting} to {photograph} .I have missed plenty of {beautiful sunsets} / {sunrises due to} being on the {spot} only five minutes before the {best} moment.",
      "cn": "在恰当的时机出现在恰当的地方，对于任何 摄影 风格而言都 至关重要 。我常常早早出发， 寻找 合适的 目的地 ，以便我能够提前准备好，避免错过我 想要拍摄 的瞬间。我曾 因为 仅在 最佳 时刻前五分钟才抵达 现场 ，而错过了很多 美丽的日落 或 日出 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "One time my friends and I drove three hours to {Devil} 's Lake, Wisconsin, to {climb} the {purple} quartz ( (石英) ) {rock} around the lake.After we found a crazy-looking {road} that hung over a {bunch} of rocks, we decided to photograph the {scene} at sunset.The position {enabled us} to look over the lake with the sunset in the {background} .We {managed} to leave this spot to climb higher because of the {spare} time until sunset.However, we did not mark the {route} so we ended up almost missing the sunset entirely. {Once} we found the place, it was stressful getting lights and {cameras} set up in the {limited} time.Still, looking back on the photos, they are some of my best shots though they could have been so much better if I had been prepared and managed my time {wisely} .",
      "cn": "有一次，我和朋友们驱车三个小时前往威斯康星州的 魔鬼 湖， 攀爬 湖边的 紫色 石英 岩 。我们发现了一条看起来相当奇特，悬在一 堆 岩石上方的 道路 后，便决定在日落时分拍摄这个 场景 。这个位置 让我们能 以日落为 背景 俯瞰湖面。由于离日落还有 多余的 时间，我们 设法 离开此地，往更高的地方攀爬。然而，我们没有标记 路线 ，结果差点完全错过了日落。 当 我们找到这个地方 时 ，在 有限的 时间内架设灯光和 相机 让人倍感压力。尽管如此，回顾这些照片，它们仍然是我最好的一些作品，尽管如果我能准备得更充分，更能 明智地 安排我的时间，本可以拍得更好。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP+Fxyt/ox+WDCb+dhfH7KaYaJ4u5RsVmLondVmcHiLum9J1BQErGzJvzqa5GEIz4ZA=="
    }
  ],
